1
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:03,741
Meet Stamp Page Designer, version seven.

2
00:00:03,791 --> 00:00:07,373
It's a free tool for making your own stamp album pages.

3
00:00:07,423 --> 00:00:13,580
Every stamp box prints at its true size, and now the tool saves the PDF for you, in one click.

4
00:00:14,386 --> 00:00:16,781
Every visit starts on the first screen.

5
00:00:16,831 --> 00:00:18,661
Continue opens your last work.

6
00:00:18,711 --> 00:00:26,745
Below it are your saved albums, and new in version seven, Open album file brings back an album you downloaded, pictures included.

7
00:00:27,550 --> 00:00:32,006
For a new album, choose the margins, the paper, and the spacing between items.

8
00:00:32,056 --> 00:00:34,432
Give it a name, and press Start designing.

9
00:00:36,010 --> 00:00:37,020
This is the editor.

10
00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:40,814
Along the top there's a button for everything you can add to a page.

11
00:00:40,864 --> 00:00:46,225
The page is in the middle, and the panel on the right shows the settings for whatever you select.

12
00:00:47,031 --> 00:00:51,081
Add a Page Header, type your title, and pick one of eighteen fonts.

13
00:00:51,131 --> 00:00:58,119
Fit the width to the text, and you can now place it in five positions: far left, left, centre, right, or far right.

14
00:00:58,169 --> 00:01:00,690
Subheaders and dividers work the same way.

15
00:01:01,492 --> 00:01:04,205
Add stamps in four sizes, or any custom size.

16
00:01:04,255 --> 00:01:06,416
Each gets an S number in its corner.

17
00:01:06,466 --> 00:01:09,425
It helps you find the stamp, and it never prints.

18
00:01:10,227 --> 00:01:12,219
Select a stamp to add its caption.

19
00:01:12,269 --> 00:01:14,682
Tick Multiple lines for up to four lines.

20
00:01:14,732 --> 00:01:19,548
Type a short note inside the frame, and tick Print it if you want it on the page.

21
00:01:19,598 --> 00:01:24,234
The frame line can be dashed or solid, for the whole album or just this stamp.

22
00:01:25,039 --> 00:01:30,392
For pocket sheets, Alt, Shift and an arrow key move an item by just over half a millimetre.

23
00:01:30,442 --> 00:01:35,618
And Exact position shows its distance from the edge of the paper, to check with a ruler.

24
00:01:36,425 --> 00:01:40,299
The Text button adds a label with no border, anywhere on the page.

25
00:01:40,349 --> 00:01:45,174
Up to four lines, with the first line bold or underlined, and any font and colour.

26
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:02,588
Clip Art now opens a chooser first.

27
00:02:02,638 --> 00:02:04,497
Nothing is added until you pick.

28
00:02:04,547 --> 00:02:13,028
There are line pictures in any colour, twenty classic stamp drawings, two hundred and fifty five flags, or your own picture from your computer.

29
00:01:45,979 --> 00:01:46,838
Frames are new.

30
00:01:46,888 --> 00:01:49,080
Select a few stamps, and press Frame.

31
00:01:49,130 --> 00:01:52,776
It fits round them, two and a half or five millimetres clear.

32
00:01:52,826 --> 00:01:57,381
Choose one, two or three lines, or a stamp edge with real perforation teeth.

33
00:01:57,431 --> 00:01:59,744
Everything inside moves with the frame.

34
00:02:13,830 --> 00:02:19,759
The Title tab sits on the corner of the page border, like the country tab on printed album pages.

35
00:02:19,809 --> 00:02:22,595
Add a flag before the text, after it, or both.

36
00:02:24,303 --> 00:02:27,913
Margin text runs up the side of the page, from bottom to top.

37
00:02:27,963 --> 00:02:31,213
You can have two on each side, each with its own flags.

38
00:02:31,263 --> 00:02:35,532
It keeps clear of the punch holes, and it isn't used with Dense margins.

39
00:02:36,334 --> 00:02:38,966
The Divider button also shows its styles first.

40
00:02:39,016 --> 00:02:41,990
Pick one, make it narrower, and choose where it sits.

41
00:02:42,793 --> 00:02:45,224
Auto-align tidies the page onto the grid.

42
00:02:45,274 --> 00:02:50,611
A frame and everything in it moves as one, and pictures and text stay where you put them.

43
00:02:50,661 --> 00:02:52,125
It never shrinks a stamp.

44
00:02:52,931 --> 00:03:01,295
The page border has new art: the Ashoka Chakra, lotus and rose, and corners with a seated lion, a beaver, a kangaroo and an eagle.

45
00:03:01,345 --> 00:03:02,913
Pick any colour you like.

46
00:03:03,715 --> 00:03:06,700
Save album keeps your work in one of three slots.

47
00:03:06,750 --> 00:03:12,151
Download album saves it as a file, with your pictures inside, so you always have a copy.

48
00:03:12,201 --> 00:03:14,134
On Safari, do this now and then.

49
00:03:14,935 --> 00:03:16,371
Now press Save as PDF.

50
00:03:16,421 --> 00:03:21,504
The tool makes the PDF itself, at true size, and saves it to your Downloads.

51
00:03:21,554 --> 00:03:22,585
No print window.

52
00:03:22,635 --> 00:03:26,232
Open it and print at one hundred percent, actual size.

53
00:03:26,282 --> 00:03:30,082
A thirty millimetre stamp gets a thirty millimetre frame.

54
00:03:30,884 --> 00:03:32,937
That's Stamp Page Designer seven.

55
00:03:32,987 --> 00:03:35,805
Free, open source, and right in your browser.

56
00:03:35,855 --> 00:03:36,888
Happy collecting!
